ther frameworks (python and other languages) are doing to fit.\r\n\r\nIt solves the issue reported where `/admin`was serving `/administrator`.\r\n\r\nEach mount path is now escaped, anchored with `(?=/|\\Z)`, and tried longest-first so the most specific mount wins, with `/` keeping its catch-all prefix semantics (#3429)\r\n\r\nCPython 3.13.5, min of 7×200k, 3 interleaved sweeps, noise floor **2.35 ns**.\r\n\r\n| scenario / probe                               | `old` | `pr`  | Δ         |\r\n| ---------------------------------------------- | ----- | ----- | --------- |\r\n| 1 mount, `/mount`                              | 90.7  | 99.4  | +8.7      |\r\n| 1 mount, `/mount/items`                        | 113.7 | 121.9 | +8.2      |\r\n| 1 mount, depth 5                               | 103.8 | 109.4 | +5.6      |\r\n| 1 mount, **miss** `/users/42/orders`           | 63.9  | 63.4  | −0.5      |\r\n| 1 mount, near-miss `/mountier/x`               | 102.6 | 72.5  | **−30.1** |\r\n| 10 mounts, hit first                           | 135.2 | 142.8 | +7.6      |\r\n| 10 mounts, hit last                            | 134.9 | 149.7 | +14.8     |\r\n| 10 mounts, **miss**                            | 66.2  | 65.3  | −0.9      |\r\n| 10 mounts, near-miss `/svcX/x`                 | 67.2  | 73.2  | +6.0      |\r\n| 50 mounts, hit first                           | 109.8 | 167.9 | **+58.1** |\r\n| 50 mounts, hit last                            | 148.8 | 191.6 | +42.8     |\r\n| 50 mounts, **miss**                            | 63.8  | 64.2  | +0.4      |\r\n| 50 mounts, near-miss `/service-xx/x`           | 130.9 | 132.1 | +1.2      |\r\n| `/`+`/admin`+`/admin/inner`+`/api`, nested hit | 96.4  | 128.4 | +32.0     |\r\n| same, `/api/v1/users`                          | 95.0  | 134.7 | +39.7     |\r\n| same, root catch-all `/anything/else`          | 96.1  | 109.3 | +13.2     |\r\n\n\n<!-- docs-preview -->\n\n<hr>\n📚 Documentation preview 📚: <a href=\"https://litestar-org.github.io/litestar-docs-preview/5178\">https://litestar-org.github.io/litestar-docs-preview/5178</a> \n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-30T07:57:46Z","updated_at":"2026-10-31T17:02:36Z","closed_at":"2026-10-31T17:02:34Z","merged_at":"2026-10-31T17:02:34Z","merge_commit_sha":"087524d38dcdb685fa55e32676cb08d692fa4fc4","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"litestar-org:fix/mount-segment-boundary","ref":"fix/mount-segment-boundary","repo":{"id":435625572,"node_id":"R_kgDOGfceZA","name":"litestar","full_name":"litestar-org/litestar","owner":{"login":"litestar-org","id":97250344,"node_id":"O_kgDOBcvsKA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97250344?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org","html_url":"https://github.com/litestar-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Light, flexible and extensible ASGI framework | Built to scale","homepage":"https://docs.litestar.dev/","language":"Python","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":["api","asgi","asyncio","litestar","litestar-api","litestar-framework","msgspec","openapi","pydantic","python","rapidoc","redoc","rest","s